ourse."] "\n\n" [:p {} "The Dutch dominated this class in the 1950s but they boycotted the 1956 Olympics, protesting the Soviet invasion of Hungary, which left the medal chase wide-open. The Oceanian boats of " [:em {} "Jest"] " (New Zealand) and " [:em {} "Falcon IV"] " (Australia) were the class of the event, winning five of the seven races. The Australian pair of " [:a {:href "/athletes/63870"} "Rolly Tasker"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/63605"} "John Scott"] " led after six races and appeared to have won the final race and the gold, but the French protested and Australia was disqualified which gave first place to New Zealand and its crew of " [:a {:href "/athletes/62885"} "Peter Mander"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/61701"} "Jack Cropp"] ". The two boats tied on total points, with 6,086, but New Zealand had won three races to Australia’s two, giving them the gold medal."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Competitors"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "Points"] [:th {} "Race #1"] [:th {} "Race #2"] [:th {} "Race #3"] [:th {} "Race #4"] [:th {} "Race #5"] [:th {} "Race #6"] [:th {} "Race #7"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {} "Jest"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/NZL"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/NZL.png"}] "NZL"]] [:td {} "6,086"] [:td {} "914 (2)"] [:td {} "1,215 (1)"] [:td {} "516 (5)"] [:td {} "613 (4)"] [:td {} "1,215 (1)"] [:td {} "1,215 (1)"] [:td {} "914 (2)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {}] [:td {:colspan "16"} [:a {:href "/athletes/62885"} "Peter Mander"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/61701"} "Jack Cropp"]]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {} "Falcon IV"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/AUS"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-c